        "id": "EX-CORE-U5-01-skill-K-HSK5-speak-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 5: speak",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Present a viewpoint with evidence, then acknowledge a plausible alternative. Mark the limits of certainty rather than presenting a preference as a proven fact.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "人际",
                "pinyin": "rénjì",
                "meaning": "human relationships; interpersonal",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "82b6267d12c98f74236dd5e97cf3916cd1d767bfd1e68c835da598eb29e66074"
              },
              {
                "text": "亲切",
                "pinyin": "qīnqiè",
                "meaning": "amiable; cordial",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "2b773fb6268d65de1c67c63e10a81cf84ed84a4a4a92f41dd188a86343e755df"
              },
              {
                "text": "虽然",
                "pinyin": "suīrán",
                "meaning": "although",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "5ca117c6cf84484e156adda4bdd4757e91606b640979bb323f4d4151dd820bd6"
              },
              {
                "text": "但是",
                "pinyin": "dànshì",
                "meaning": "but; however",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "1fac104a345a55d1bf1705e3cb2765411e111844ef0ed8389208c90fc1d31949"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A new member can meet a helpful acquaintance today or a close relative tomorrow. The acquaintance has already offered help today; the relative has not replied. You prefer today because of the explicit offer. Acknowledge the alternative and the fact that silence does not establish unwillingness.\nFamiliar meanings available: human relationships; interpersonal; amiable; cordial; although; but; however."
          }
        ]
      },
